From b209da8cdac62419a1c6495abf79323e6961e14a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stew675 <stew675@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:26:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip: reporting audit + a measured transport selector (the
 ping-pong becomes the default at prefill width)

Session 4 of the flash-next-prefill campaign (wip/flash-next-prefill/HANDOVER-session4.md).

REPORTING AUDIT (the maintainer's ask): every printed arena number now says which of the four
kinds it is.  SLAB_STATS gains arena_region= (mapped - boundary, an EXTENT), arena_resident=
(the same figure the MoE census calls resident=), transport= / transport_used= (the slab CARVE and
its USAGE, renamed from ring=) and SLAB_INIT prints transport_req=.  The MoE census' 'arena=' was
RESIDENT bytes and is now 'resident= ... total'; the fill census' 'arena=' was BYTES COPIED from the
arena and is now 'arena_copies=' (with 'host_copies=' and 'H2D % of filled'); 'prefill cache staging'
is 'prefill fills'.  Every field is defined in one comment block at the log site.  The transport
region is now sized from what the ping-pong holds (N x the largest host-weight SPLIT SET, a new
llama_model::max_host_expert_layer_bytes) instead of the deleted ring's throughput knee: 6618 MiB ->
3412 MiB on the 89k Flash-Next shape, and the freed band is visible (+3.2 GiB of arena region during
the prefill, 25 GiB of fills served from the arena instead of the host; same text, same rate).
Env renames with deprecated aliases: GGML_CUDA_SLAB_TRANSPORT_MIB (was _RING_MIB) and
GGML_CUDA_SLAB_TRANSPORT_FALLBACK.

TENSOR SPLIT FIXES (2 and 3 cards could not run this shape at all):
 * the VMM workspace pool aborted on a failed growth ('HipVMM Failure: out of memory'); on a refused
   cuMemCreate it now takes the scratch from the slab's wide band (fail-soft, the optional-transient
   rule) and names the sizes if there is no band either.  This was the -sm tensor 2-card blocker at
   BOTH transports (gather and staged).
 * the scheduler ping-pong is declined on a Meta backend (a split IS the whole graph there and the
   slot API does not exist) instead of calling a NULL stage_buffer: SIGSEGV -> the split uses its own
   per-device ring via stage_input.

TRANSPORT SELECTOR: sched_stage_exposure_decides() stages a pool-backed host table at prefill width
when the bytes the device gather would pull over the link per token clear a threshold, and keeps the
gather when the set is resident.  Threshold 38 us/token from a measured sweep (coverage 30 / 45 / 56 %
on 35B-A3B Q8_0 + Flash-Next at 51 %; the tie is 8.8 GB / 8192 tok at 28.7 GB/s).  The slab's
zero-carve rule is re-keyed to the same measurement (carve only when the cache cannot keep the set),
because a zero-carve slab refuses every fill and dropped the arm to 338 t/s.

Measured (89k prompt, heat prior pinned, same seed, 3 rotated cycles where quoted): 1 GPU 2108 -> 2445
(+16 %, text 43d0b1f4629e); 2-card tensor split (0,2) 3419 with the gather (unchanged, +13 % over the
split's staged arm); 3-card tensor 3201 (unchanged); 2-card layer split 2475 (unchanged); 122B-A10B
1 GPU 961 -> 1036 (+7.8 %, text c3f4da781f01).  GGML_SCHED_STAGE_SELECT=0 restores the pre-session
rule; GGML_SCHED_STAGE_EXPOSE_US tunes the threshold.
